  "approach": "Teach the names of languages (lowercase, masculine, no article after hablar) and the demonyms for well-known cities and regions, including the ones a learner hears in conversation (porteño, chilango, boricua).",
  "coverage": [
    "Languages are lowercase and masculine: el español, el inglés, el francés, el portugués",
    "After hablar the article is usually dropped: Hablo inglés y español",
    "Español and castellano both name Spanish",
    "City and region demonyms: madrileño (Madrid), bogotano (Bogotá), limeño (Lima), porteño (Buenos Aires)",
    "Informal ones heard often: chilango (Mexico City), boricua (Puerto Rican)",
    "Porteño usually means from Buenos Aires; in Chile it can mean from Valparaíso",
    "Ella es porteña: demonyms agree like nationalities"
  ],
